# The kernel patch series for Dolby Vision and HDR10+ on HDMI.
#
# It fits Linux 7.3. kernel/apply-series.sh applies the lines in order.
#
#   upstream PATH SHA256  a file of libreelec-x86-DV at UPSTREAM_COMMIT in
#                         kernel/upstream.conf, with its checksum
#   local FILE            a file in kernel/patches/
#
# Order: the upstream project applies its patches in file name order, with
# the patches of packages/linux/patches/default/ first. The series keeps
# that order, because later patches build on earlier ones.
#
# Left out:
#   0102-wifi-mt76-*, 0103-wifi-mt76-*, 0104-wifi-mt76-*, 0062-imon-*,
#     9901-pm-*: no relation to video
#   linux-9920, 9921, 9925, 9930, 9946, 9947, 9970, 9971, 9972, 9975, 9977,
#     9978: AMD display. The project targets Intel GPUs.
#   linux-9950-*: support for newer Intel chips (Wildcat Lake, Panther Lake).
#     Two of them are part of Linux 7.3 already.
#   linux-9973, 9974, 9976: player-led Dolby Vision (LLDV) for more Intel
#     chips and formats. The CB1 mpv has no player-led output.

